[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Night Vision - Configurable[/color][/b][/size]

See in the dark with a [b]neutral white-light radius[/b] around your character or [b]Fullscreen[/b] brightness. Add a softly fading vampire vignette, black-and-white shading or red tint in [b]5% steps[/b].

Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/294]Night Vision by opogode[/url], [b]made with permission[/b].

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Controls[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Keyboard:[/color][/b] Press N to toggle night vision in vampire form.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller:[/color][/b] Hold L3 / the left stick for 0.6 seconds. Release between toggles.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Stays on until you turn it off[/color][/b][/size]

Once enabled, vision stays on until you toggle it off or return to human form. Loading a save or switching player or camera preserves your choice and automatically resumes the effect when ready. A new game session starts with vision off. A brief brightness pulse marks Fullscreen activation.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Open [b]Mod Settings > Night Vision - Configurable[/b]. Press Apply to save changes and adjust active vision immediately.

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Enabled:[/color][/b] Enables the mod; switching it Off also turns vision off. Enabling it again does not activate vision automatically. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Night Vision Mode:[/color][/b] Radius lights the area around you like a white torch. Fullscreen brightens the whole view. Default: Fullscreen.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Light radius:[/color][/b] 5–50 metres in 1-metre steps. Shown only in Radius mode. Default: 6 metres.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vignette:[/color][/b] Soft red veins from the game's vampire blood-hunger texture. Hidden in menus; does not trigger hunger or damage effects. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vignette opacity:[/color][/b] 0–100% strength in 5% steps. Shown only with Vignette On. Default: 20%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Black & White:[/color][/b] 0% keeps natural colours; 100% is black and white. Adjustable in 5% steps. Default: 0%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Red tint:[/color][/b] 0–100% in 5% steps. Colours only the added light in Radius mode, or the whole view in Fullscreen mode. The border stays red independently. Default: 0%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Brightness:[/color][/b] 25–300% in 5% steps. 100% is normal game brightness in Fullscreen mode, or standard light strength in Radius mode. Default: 200%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller shortcut:[/color][/b] Enables the left-stick hold. Keyboard N remains available. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Writes setup, activation and aggregate diagnostics to ue4ss/UE4SS.log. Default: Off.
[/list]

Without the menu, close the game, edit NightVisionConfigurable/settings.ini after it has been generated on first launch, and restart. The included settings.ini.example lists the defaults.

Menus temporarily hide all vision effects; returning to gameplay restores them without another toggle. Pausing, showing the cursor, blocking movement or hiding gameplay UI also suspends the effects and shortcuts. Turning vision off removes the light and border and restores camera values still owned by the mod. No extra bloom or chromatic aberration is added.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Night-Vision-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Data/NightVisionConfigurable folder into <The Blood of Dawnwalker>/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

